[ORIGINAL PLAN]
STEP 1
navigator: wait (stay still so sensors can run)
lidar: sense range + report any centroids (looking for container class 58)
camera: look at RGB image / record view
STEP 2
navigator: IF STEP 1 returned a container centroid -> drive to the computed approach point that stays >= 3.0 m from that centroid (goal = centroid + 3*(pose - centroid)/||pose - centroid|| using current robot pose). ELSE -> drive to free occupancy cell (6, 6) to get a new viewpoint.
lidar: wait while navigator moves
camera: look while moving / record frames
STEP 3
navigator: wait (stop and stabilize)
lidar: sense range + report any centroids (looking for container class 58)
camera: look at RGB image
STEP 4
navigator: IF STEP 3 returned a container centroid -> drive to the computed approach point that stays >= 3.0 m from that centroid (use formula above). ELSE -> drive to another free occupancy cell (-6, -6) to continue searching.
lidar: wait while navigator moves
camera: look while moving
STEP 5
navigator: wait (stop and stabilize at the approach)
lidar: sense range + report centroids; IF a container centroid is now sensed and Q1 is in valid approach pose -> confirm_stop("container") to record the container visit. (If still no centroid, return to STEP 4/3 loop.)
camera: capture image of the stopped viewpoint
STEP 6
navigator: wait (do not move until container is confirmed)
lidar: once container is confirmed, sense to start search for rock (class 40) and report any rock centroids
camera: look at RGB image
STEP 7
navigator: IF a rock centroid is reported -> drive to the computed approach point that stays >= 3.0 m from that rock centroid (use centroid → approach formula). ELSE -> drive to a free occupancy cell opposite the container search area (example free cell: (6, -6)) to get a new viewpoint for rock search.
lidar: wait while navigator moves
camera: look while moving
STEP 8
navigator: wait (stop and stabilize)
lidar: sense range + report any centroids (looking for rock class 40)
camera: look at RGB image
STEP 9
navigator: IF STEP 8 returned a rock centroid -> drive to the computed approach point that stays >= 3.0 m from that rock centroid (use formula above). ELSE -> drive to another free occupancy cell (choose a different quadrant) and continue searching.
lidar: wait while navigator moves
camera: look while moving
STEP 10
navigator: wait (stop and stabilize at the approach)
lidar: sense range + report centroids; IF a rock centroid is sensed and Q1 is in valid approach pose -> confirm_stop("rock") to record the rock visit. (If still no centroid, return to STEP 9/8 loop.)
camera: capture image of the stopped viewpoint
STEP 11
navigator: wait
lidar: final check that both container and rock have been confirmed; if any confirmation is missing, resume the appropriate search steps above (container search before rock). Otherwise report both confirmed.
camera: capture final images / prepare report
STEP 12
FINISHED

